    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="introduction" tabindex="-1">Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction&quot;">​</a></h1><p>zkde.fi is a Starknet application for privacy-aware, policy-governed DeFi execution. It is designed for two audiences at the same time:</p><ul><li>users who want practical control over private and verifiable execution</li><li>integrators building GATE-aligned workflows on top of exposed APIs and standards</li></ul><h2 id="the-problem-this-solves" tabindex="-1">The Problem This Solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-problem-this-solves" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Problem This Solves&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Most DeFi systems force a tradeoff between privacy and operational trust. Either everything is public and strategy leaks, or the flow is opaque and users cannot independently verify that policy constraints were honored.</p><h2 id="why-this-matters" tabindex="-1">Why This Matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-this-matters" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why This Matters&quot;">​</a></h2><p>For users, this tradeoff creates avoidable risk and friction. For integrators, it makes it difficult to reason about external automation safety and auditability when linking real capital flows.</p><h2 id="what-zkde-fi-combines" tabindex="-1">What zkde.fi Combines <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-zkde-fi-combines" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What zkde.fi Combines&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Policy-aware execution controls in a user-facing app</li><li>Proof and receipt pathways that vary by flow type</li><li>Session-based delegation for constrained automation</li><li>Selective disclosure for verifier-facing claims</li><li>Risk and trust context surfaced in Profile and Passport views</li></ul><h2 id="flow-specific-proof-model-important" tabindex="-1">Flow-Specific Proof Model (Important) <a class="header-anchor" href="#flow-specific-proof-model-important" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Flow-Specific Proof Model (Important)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Proof behavior is flow-dependent. zkde.fi does not frame all actions as identical.</p><ul><li>Some paths are fully gate-critical and require strict proof/receipt confirmation before execution acceptance.</li><li>Some paths are advisory or policy-preview oriented and may return risk signals without hard blocking.</li><li>Some operational paths rely on wallet-authorized execution with post-action state reconciliation.</li></ul><p>This flow-specific model reflects production reality and avoids over-promising a single “one size fits all” proof mode.</p><div class="language-mermaid vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">mermaid</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">flowchart LR</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  A[User intent] --&gt; B{Execution path}</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  B --&gt;|Gate-critical| C[Proof + policy enforcement]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  B --&gt;|Advisory| D[Risk signal + recommendation]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  B --&gt;|Wallet-first| E[Signed execution + reconciliation]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  C --&gt; F[Receipt trail]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  D --&gt; F</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  E --&gt; F</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="surfaces-you-will-use" tabindex="-1">Surfaces You Will Use <a class="header-anchor" href="#surfaces-you-will-use" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Surfaces You Will Use&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>/agent</code> for execution surfaces (<code>vault</code>, <code>trade</code>, <code>brain</code>)</li><li><code>/profile</code> for trust, reputation, compliance, and connections</li><li><code>/docs</code> for operational and integration references</li></ul><h2 id="production-and-experimental-scope" tabindex="-1">Production And Experimental Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#production-and-experimental-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Production And Experimental Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These docs intentionally include both production and experimental capabilities. Pages identify when a flow is stable versus rapidly evolving so users and integrators can make informed decisions about adoption risk.</p><p>Next: <a href="/docs/why.html">Why zkde.fi?</a> | <a href="/docs/concepts.html">Concepts</a> | <a href="/docs/quick-start.html">Quick start</a></p>', 19)
